---
# The API reference layout: the Astro routes render through StarlightPage with `tableOfContents: false`, so the
# frame is the article chrome of base.liquid (header, the sidebar column, footer) and <main> holds
# partials/page-content (the title with the `api-page-title` class and the page actions, then the content and the
# footer). The route templates of content/reference/api/ capture `title` and `description` and render their own
# breadcrumbs (templates/api/breadcrumb.liquid; partials/breadcrumbs is off on API pages) and the in-page search.
# `api_page` switches the chrome to the API reference: partials/sidebar renders templates/api/sidebar.liquid with the
# API collapse/expand buttons, head.liquid uses the default social image.
# The other values are the StarlightPage frontmatter of the Astro routes (prev/next: false, pagefind: false); Starlight
# showed no edit link there (a generated page has no source file).
layout: base.liquid
has_sidebar: true
has_toc: false
api_page: true
pagefind: false
prev: false
next: false
editUrl: false
---
{%- include "partials/page-vars" -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The API components' scoped styles (scripts/client/api/extract-styles.mjs); site.css holds api-reference.css.
  Linked before the content so it applies before the first paint of the panels below.
{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/api-components.css">
{% include "partials/page-content" %}
{%- comment -%}
  The API search controllers (scripts/client/api/index.js imports the one of each search root). The page's own
  controller (`api_search` front matter) is also a module script of the document, after index.js (module scripts run
  in order, so the version filters are restored first; the dynamic import then resolves to the same module): the
  load event waits for it, so a chip clicked once the page has loaded is never lost to a controller still loading.
{%- endcomment %}
<script type="module" src="/scripts/client/api/index.js"></script>
{%- if api_search %}
<script type="module" src="/scripts/client/api/{{ api_search }}.js"></script>
{%- endif %}
